\n   Each \\(\\ell_c\\) is parallel to the forbidden line \\(x+y=0\\) and therefore non\u2011sunny.  \n   The line \\(\\ell_c\\) contains exactly the lattice points with \\(a+b=c\\); thus the collection \\(\\{\\ell_c\\}_{c=2}^{n+1}\\) covers every point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\).\n\n   *Construction for an arbitrary \\(k\\) with \\(1\\le k\\le n-2\\).*  \n   - **Step\u202f1 (sunny lines).**  \n     Choose \\(k\\) distinct integers \\(s_1,\\dots ,s_k\\) from \\(\\{1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}\\).  \n     For each \\(i\\) pick a slope \\(\\alpha_i\\) different from \\(0,\\infty,-1\\) and from the slopes already used; for definiteness set  \n\n     \\[\n     \\alpha_i:=\\frac{1}{i+1}\\qquad(i=1,\\dots ,k).\n     \\]\n\n     Define the sunny line  \n\n     \\[\n     S_i:\\; y-1=\\alpha_i\\,(x-s_i).\n     \\]\n\n     The line \\(S_i\\) passes through the point \\((s_i,1)\\) of the bottom row and, because \\(\\alpha_i\\notin\\{0,\\infty,-1\\}\\), it is sunny.  \n     The \\(k\\) chosen abscissae \\(s_i\\) are distinct, so the \\(k\\) sunny lines are distinct.\n\n   - **Step\u202f2 (non\u2011sunny lines).**  \n     The remaining points of the bottom row are the \\(n-k\\) points  \n\n     \\[\n     (t,1)\\qquad t\\in T:=\\{1,2,\\dots ,n\\}\\setminus\\{s_1,\\dots ,s_k\\}.\n     \\]\n\n     For each \\(t\\in T\\) introduce the vertical line  \n\n     \\[\n     V_t:\\;x=t .\n     \\]\n\n     Every \\(V_t\\) is parallel to the \\(y\\)-axis, hence non\u2011sunny.  \n     The set \\(\\{V_t\\mid t\\in T\\}\\) consists of exactly \\(n-k\\) distinct lines.\n\n   - **Step\u202f3 (verification of the covering property).**  \n     *Bottom row.*  \n     By construction each point \\((s_i,1)\\) lies on the sunny line \\(S_i\\), and each point \\((t,1)\\) with \\(t\\in T\\) lies on the vertical line \\(V_t\\). Hence all points of \\(R\\) are covered.\n\n     *Higher rows.*  \n     Let \\((a,b)\\) be any lattice point with \\(a,b\\ge1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\).  \n     If 