re obtained by the same recipe with the appropriate choice of the initial non\u2011sunny set.\n\n---\n\n**2. Detailed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nT_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z_{>0}^2\\mid a+b\\le n+1\\}\n\\]\n\nbe the set of lattice points that have to be covered.  \nRecall that a line is **sunny** iff its direction vector is not parallel to \\((1,0)\\), \\((0,1)\\) or \\((1,-1)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma\u202f1  \n*For any integer \\(m\\ge 1\\) the family*\n\n\\[\n\\mathcal V_m=\\{x=i\\mid 1\\le i\\le m\\},\\qquad \n\\mathcal H_m=\\{y=j\\mid 1\\le j\\le m\\}\n\\]\n\n*covers all points of \\(T_{2m-1}\\) except those belonging to the two diagonals*\n\n\\[\nD_1=\\{(a,\\,2m-a)\\mid 1\\le a\\le m\\},\\qquad \nD_2=\\{(a,\\,2m-1-a)\\mid 1\\le a\\le m-1\\}.\n\\]\n\n**Proof.**  \nTake any \\((a,b)\\in T_{2m-1}\\). If \\(a\\le m\\) then the vertical line \\(x=a\\) (which belongs to \\(\\mathcal V_m\\)) contains the point.  \nIf \\(a>m\\) then \\(b\\le 2m-1-a < m\\); hence the horizontal line \\(y=b\\) (which belongs to \\(\\mathcal H_m\\)) contains the point.  \nThe only points for which neither inequality holds are those with \\(a\\le m\\) and \\(b\\le m\\) simultaneously and with equality \\(a+b=2m\\) or \\(a+b=2m-1\\); these are precisely the points of \\(D_1\\cup D_2\\). \u220e\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma\u202f2  \n*Let \\(r\\ge 1\\). The set*\n\n\\[\nB_r=\\{(a,b)\\in T_{2r}\\mid a+b\\in\\{2r,2r+1\\}\\}\n\\]\n\n*is contained in a single sunny line.*\n\n**Proof.**  \nAll points of \\(B_r\\) satisfy the linear equation  \n\n\\[\nx+y=2r\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+y=2r+1 .\n\\]\n\nPick any two distinct points of \\(B_r\\) that lie on different of the two parallel lines, for instance \\((1,2r-1)\\) and \\((1,2r)\\). The line through them has equation  \n\n\\[\ny = (2r-1)+(x-1)=x+2r-2,\n\\]\n\ni.e. slope \\(1\\). Its direction vector \\((1,1)\\) is not parallel to \\((1