a\\) with \\(a\\le n-1\\) then \\(|C_a|\\ge 2\\). By Lemma\u202f2 a\nnon\u2011vertical line cannot contain two points of such a column; by Lemma\u202f1 each\nsunny line can contribute at most one point to the column. Hence a column with\n\\(|C_a|\\ge 2\\) cannot be completely covered unless it possesses its own vertical\nline. Therefore the only column that may be left without a vertical line is\n\\(C_n\\), which consists of the single point \\((n,1)\\).\n\nThus the number of columns that are not assigned a vertical line is at most one,\nand each of those columns can be covered by at most one sunny line. Hence  \n\n\\[\nk\\le 1 .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Conclusion\n\nWe have exhibited explicit configurations for \\(k=0\\) and for \\(k=1\\), and we have\nproved that any admissible configuration must satisfy \\(k\\le 1\\). Therefore the\nset of admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
